      "biography": {
        "value": "<h2>Description</h2><p>A juvenile ochu. This round little monster looks adorable todding around, but it would not do to forget that it is still an ochu. The diminutive microchu can move quickly and they often travel in packs, which means that travelers can easily find themselves surrounded by enemies if they do not keep a weather eye out. And where you find microchus, you find ochus not far behind. It is altogether safer to avoid these cute critters whenever possible.</p><h2>Defense</h2><p>AC 16, touch 14, flat-footed 13 (+2 natural, +3 dex, +1 size)</p><p>hp 25 [36] (3d8+12)</p><p>Fort +6, Ref +4, Will +1</p><p>Immune Plant traits; Resist Lightning 5, Ice 5, Water 5</p><p>Weakness Fire and Earth</p><h2>Offense</h2><p>Speed 30 ft., Burrow 10 ft., Climb 20 ft.</p><p>Melee Bite +4 (1d4+1)</p><p>Special Attacks Critical Attack, Photosynthesis, Plead</p><h2>Statistics</h2><p>Str 12, Dex 16, Con 16, Int 2, Wis 10, Cha 6</p><p>Base Atk +2; CMB +2; CMD 15</p><p>Feats Alertness, Toughness</p><p>Skills Climb +5, Perception +4, Stealth +10 (+14 in vegetation); Racial Modifiers +4 Climb</p>"
      }
